  "id": "COMPOUND:35454 - PROTEIN:6326",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that (8S,8a-R)-7-Deacetyl-1,O8,8,8a-tetrahydro-7-epi-sclerotiorin may interact with Phosphodiesterase 6C through multiple indirect pathways. This compound is identified as a target of several molecules, including Lancifodilactone G and 3,3'-bis(3,4-dihydro-4-hydroxy-6-methoxy-2H-1-benzopyran), which in turn target Phosphodiesterase 6C. Additionally, the compound is also a target of 2-Methylpropanoyl 2-Methylpropanoate, which also leads to Phosphodiesterase 6C. These findings indicate that the compound may exert its biological effects through a series of downstream targets, potentially modulating Phosphodiesterase 6C activity. The evidence is consistent with a mechanism involving the activation or inhibition of Phosphodiesterase 6C, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
